# REST Client (VS Code: humao.rest-client). Start the app first: npm run dev
# Exercise C: the tenant and the permissions must come from the session, not from the body.
# Before Exercise C the tamper and viewer calls return 200 (that is the bug) and the control call
# returns 400 (tenantId is still required). After Exercise C: tamper and viewer calls return 403,
# and the control returns 200 because the tenant now comes from the session.

@api = http://localhost:3000

### Login as alice (analyst, acme)
# @name alice
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@acme" }

### Login as carol (viewer, acme)
# @name carol
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "carol@acme" }

### Tamper: alice asks the assistant about globex (expected after C: 403)
POST {{api}}/api/assistant
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.token}}

{ "question": "Summarize performance and highlight key risks.", "tenantId": "globex" }

### Tamper: alice fetches the globex risk report (expected after C: 403)
POST {{api}}/api/data/report
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.token}}

{ "tenantId": "globex" }

### Viewer: carol asks the assistant (expected after C: 403, viewers cannot read risk reports)
POST {{api}}/api/assistant
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.token}}

{ "question": "Summarize performance and highlight key risks.", "tenantId": "acme" }

### Viewer: carol fetches the acme risk report (expected after C: 403)
POST {{api}}/api/data/report
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.token}}

{ "tenantId": "acme" }

### Control: alice without tenantId (before C: 400; after C: 200, acme taken from the session)
POST {{api}}/api/assistant
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.token}}

{ "question": "Summarize performance and highlight key risks." }
